Page=new Array();Page[0]=new Array("A Derived Data Script is used to create new derived variable values by applying mathematical, logical or string manipulation operations to existing logical data source characteristics. A script can be used to transform existing data, perform calculations, derive new permanent data characteristics, or modify the value of existing data characteristics.","A derived data script may be written as:","'Residual Income' = 'Net Monthly Income' - 'Monthly Outgoings'","For each record processed through the script, data values will be calculated for the characteristic <br>'Residual Income' from the input data supplied in characteristics 'Net Monthly income' and 'Monthly Outgoings'","For example: 'Net Monthly Income' = 1200, 'Monthly Outgoings' = 1000","therefore 'Residual Income' = 1200-1000 = 200.","The characteristic for which values are being derived must already exist in the logical data source.","The user creates scripts by entering text into a script editor where mathematical, logical or string manipulation operations are applied to logical data source characteristics, (Operators and functions).  ","The script editor displays characteristic names, operators, command verbs, etc., in different colours. ","The script editor has basic text manipulation such as selecting blocks of text to cut, copy, paste and delete.","As the script must follow certain syntax rules there is an option to check the syntax of the script. For guidelines on some of the script syntax rules see Guidelines on script syntax.","The script syntax must be valid before any testing can be carried out. ","Derived Data Scripts overview","DerivedDataScriptsoverview.htm");
Page[1]=new Array("The Derived Data Script editor enables the user to define a derived data script using script either by adding the script freehand to the editor or by using the required resources from the Palette and Resources window. ","The derived data script editor consists of:","Derived data script tool bar with options designed to assist the user in defining a derived data script.","Script editor - area of the editor where script can be typed in freehand or resources can be dragged and dropped into the editor from the Palette and Resources window.  The editor also indicates in the right hand bar which line is currently being edited. Line wrapping can be enabled for the scripting editor from within the Tools menu.","Search window - area below the editor where the user can locate a logical data source characteristic. If the window is not displayed, click on the window expander @ on the bottom edge of the editor to display it.","In the Search field @ type the word or part of a word that makes up the name of the characteristic.<br>The Select Characteristic dialog will focus in on a particular characteristic or set of characteristics that match this word.","If the Select Characteristic dialog is displaying the characteristics in a tree view, the logical data source will need to be fully expanded to see all the characteristics that match the word(s).","The characteristic itself must be selected from the Resources window for use in the script.","Derived Data Script editor","DerivedDataScripteditor.htm");
Page[2]=new Array("The Derived Data Script editor's tool bar is used to assist the user in defining a derived data script.","@ Compile Script - checks the script for syntax errors ","@ Test - launches the Interactive Tester for the derived data script","@ Last Edit - takes the user to the line of the script where editing last took place","@ Find Selection - select to locate a highlighted section of script. Find Selection can be used in conjunction with Ctrl + F to search within a script","@ Find Previous Occurrence - select to locate the previous occurrence of a highlighted section of script","@ Find Next Occurrence - select to locate the next occurrence of a highlighted section of script","@ Toggle Highlight Search - select to highlight all the occurrences of the highlighted section of script","@ Toggle Rectangular Selection - click to enable your cursor to select a rectangular selection.  A useful tool for copying areas of script.","@ Shift Line Left - moves the whole line to the left by one tab stop","@ Shift Line Right - moves the whole line to the right by one tab stop","Derived Data Script editor tool bar","DerivedDataScripteditortoolbar.htm");
Page[3]=new Array("By default, line wrapping in the scripting editor is enabled to wrap lines at word breaks. If desired, the user can modify line wrapping from within the Tools main menu.","To modify line wrapping in the scripting editor","Select Options from the Tools main menu.","From the Editor options, click on the Formatting tab.","From the Line Wrap menu, select a line wrap option. Choices are:","Off - turns line wrapping off.","After Words - the line will wrap after a word.","Anywhere - the line will wrap at the right edge of the window, regardless of where the break occurs in the line.","The results are displayed in the Preview window: ","Click OK to save the setting.","Line wrapping will now be modified in the scripting editor.","Line wrapping in the scripting editor","Linewrappinginthescriptingeditor.htm");
Page[4]=new Array("A derived data script can be created from the Explorer window. ","You will only be able to add a component type that has been allowed for the selected folder. If it is not allowed it will not be listed and therefore cannot be selected. ","To create a derived data script ","From the Explorer window right click at the required folder level and select Add component.","Select Derived Data Script.","In the Create component dialog enter the name of the derived data script.","If you wish to have the new component display in the Main editor on creation, ensure that the Open new components in component editor tick box is selected.","Click on the OK button.","The derived data script editor will open allowing you to edit script, compile and test the derived data script.<br>The derived data script name will be listed in the Explorer window under the selected folder level. The component is identified by the @ icon.","If you do not wish the editor to open, de-select the tick box. From the Explorer window select the derived data script and select Open. ","Create a derived data script","Createaderiveddatascript.htm");
Page[5]=new Array("The scripting language provides for the following templates in derived data scripts and user defined functions.","Evaluate ... When","Repeat ... Until","If...","While ... Do","If ... Then ... Else","Templates","Templates.htm");
Page[6]=new Array("Editing a script involves entering the script content using the correct language and according to the correct syntax and grammar. Scripts can be edited, compiled and tested in a script editor. ","See the topic Operators and functions for details of the operators, functions and statements that can be used in the script editor.","To edit a derived data script","With the derived data script editor open you can add script freehand or using the required resources from the Resources window you can.","Add a characteristic to a script","Add an operator or function to a script","Add a boolean expression to a script","Add a class set to a script","Add a template to a script","Click on the Compile Script @ button to check the script.","The derived data script can now be used within other components.","Edit a derived data script","Editaderiveddatascript.htm");
Page[7]=new Array("Invalid script syntax will prevent the component for which the script is written to be tested or processed correctly. The deployment validation will prevent this from ever happening.","The following are some guidelines on entering script in the script editor.","A single space should be entered to separate each function, operator, characteristic or value entered.","A space must be added after a function/operator name (e.g., OR) but is not required after a symbol. However, spaces are recommended for readability.","A return should not be placed on the last line of the script.","To be able to use double quotes (or any non-alphanumeric characters) in string evaluations within a script, the user will need to use the \\ (escape) to differentiate between delimiters for the string and the contents of the string when double quotes are used.  <br>For example, if a class set returns &quot;Married&quot; (including the quotes) as the full interval name (this would occur if the Set all interval name to default icon @ is selected), to be able to use &quot;Married&quot; in a boolean expression the following would need to be entered. ","Guidelines on script syntax","Guidelinesonscriptsyntax.htm");
Page[8]=new Array("When the user first drags a function into a script the places intended for the variables are marked by short expressions such as '&lt;expr&gt;' or '&lt;stmt&gt;'. The meaning of these expressions are as follows:","Expression","Meaning","array","The array characteristic that you want to perform the function on","base","The base of the logarithm to be calculated","char","In a function on a string characteristic, the name of the characteristic on which the function is to be performed","const","A whole number or a piece of script that returns a constant value","date","In a DAYOFWEEK function, the date for which the day of the week is to be found","date1","In a DAYS or MONTHS function, the date normally expected to be the earlier of the two, i.e. that will lead to a positive number being returned if it is the earliest","date2","In a DAYS or MONTHS function, the date normally expected to be later of the two, i.e. that leads to a positive number being returned if it is the latest","dest","In a function operating on an array, the new array that is to be created by the function, containing the sorted or merged array(s)","divisor","The number by which you want to divide (or a piece of script that returns that number)","expr","Any piece of script that returns either true or false or a number","givendate","In a DATE function, the known date from which an unknown date is to be found (or a piece of script that returns that date)","length","In a SUBSTRING function, the length of the substring to be taken","modality","The characteristic that will hold the number of modes","modalValues","The characteristic that will hold a list of the modes","multiple","In a rounding function, the input is rounded to a number divisible by the multiple","order","In a sort function, a letter code that denotes how the array is to be sorted","period","In a DATE function, the number of days after the given date that the date to be found is (or a piece of script that returns that number)","start","In a SUBSTRING function, the position in the original string of the first character of the substring","stmt","Any piece of script that performs a task, such as assigning a value to one or more characteristics","tail","In topping and tailing; the number of the highest entries to ignore","top","In topping and tailing; the number of lowest entries to ignore","toptaildev","In topping and tailing by standard deviations; the number of standard deviations from the mean outside of which values should be ignored","value","The individual value that is to be found in the given array (or a piece of script that returns that value)","value1","In a STRING function, the character string that will form the first part of the new string (or a piece of script that returns that string)","value2","In a STRING function, the character string that will form the second part of the new string (or a piece of script that returns that string)","Placeholders in functions","Placeholdersinfunctions.htm");
Page[9]=new Array("The script editor must be open for editing.","To add a characteristic using auto complete","Press Ctrl+Space to display the list of all available logical data sources and functions. ","or","Press the quote (') key to display only the list of available logical data sources.","Use the down arrow or mouse to select a data source from the list, and press enter. The data source is added to the script.","With the cursor positioned after the data source name, press the full stop key (.) to display the list of available characteristics:","Use the down arrow or mouse to select a characteristic from the list, and press enter. The characteristic is added to the script.","If the selected characteristic contains further child characteristics (such characteristics are identified by not having a closing quote (') after the name), you can again press the full stop key (.) to display the list of available characteristics.","If the selected characteristic is an array characteristic (such characteristics are identified by brackets [ ] after the name), you can position the cursor inside the brackets and then use auto completion to add a characteristic for the index, if dynamic indexing is required (as opposed to using static, constant numbers).","To add a characteristic to a script from the Resources window","Click on the Expand (+) button to display the contents of the logical data source in the Resources window.","Drag the required logical data source and drop it onto the script at the required position.","The Select Characteristic dialog opens","In the Search field @ type the word or part of a word that makes up the name of the characteristic.<br>The Select Characteristic dialog will focus in on a particular characteristic or set of characteristics that match this word.","If the Select Characteristic dialog is displaying the characteristics in a tree view, the logical data source will need to be fully expanded to see all the characteristics that match the word(s).","Select the characteristic you require.","Click on the OK button. The Select Characteristic dialog closes and the characteristics you have selected will be added.","To add a characteristic to a script freehand","Enter the name of the characteristic.","Characteristics must always be in single quotes (including the logical data source name).","To add an array characteristic to a script using drag and drop","You can add an array characteristic to a script using auto complete, or you can use drag and drop as described here. Drag and drop is appropriate primarily for adding constant arrays (see Declaring characteristics variables within a script for more on this).","Click on the Expand (+) button to display the contents of the logical data source in the Resources window.","Drag the required logical data source and drop it onto the script at the required position.","The Select Characteristic dialog opens.","Locate the required array element and click on the OK button.","when selecting a leaf characteristic array, the syntax will be:<br>'temp.data[1]' ","when selecting a leaf characteristic array within a group array, the syntax will be:<br>'temp.array[1].data[1]'","the above syntax examples can be manually changed to use other characteristics to define the desired array index. See following syntax example:","'temp.array'['temp.index1'].'data['temp.index2']'","The Select Characteristic dialog will close and the array characteristic you have chosen will be added to the script.","Add a characteristic to a script","Addacharacteristictoascript.htm");
Page[10]=new Array("There are two ways to add an array characteristic to a script: by dragging and dropping from the Resources window, and by using auto complete. Currently, the two methods use different syntaxes, each of which is valid in its proper context.","Using drag and drop","Using drag and drop to add an array characteristic invokes the Select Characteristic dialog; this allows the user to select a constant array, as in this example:","'Application.applicant[1].staticleafarray[2]'  ","This syntax will only support constant values; dropping in another characteristic as an array index will result in a syntax error. Consequently, using drag and drop is inappropriate for creating dynamic arrays. ","Using auto complete","Using auto complete, the array characteristic has the following format:","'Application.applicant'[1].'Account'[1]","By including an array index, the same syntax is used for dynamic arrays:  ","'Application.applicant'[1].'Account'['Application.index']","Currently, both syntax formats are supported in the software. In future, however, only the syntax followed by the auto complete feature may be supported, as it allows for a richer, more flexible user experience.","Declaring characteristic variables within scripts","Declaringcharacteristicvariableswithinscripts.htm");
Page[11]=new Array("Arrays are specified in the logical data source and logical data model editors by setting the array size to *. This setting is available for all characteristics within the editor. The following is an example of a dynamic group and leaf characteristic definition:","Leaf characteristics","The array length from the size function can be used to iterate through a dynamic array. ","In this example, Input.Balances is a dynamic array. If the dynamic array has not been dimensioned (e.g. by using a CSV file in Interactive Tester) then the SIZE function will return 1 and 1 iteration of the loop will be performed.","'Input.size' = SIZE( 'Input.Balances' )","'Input.index' = 1","WHILE 'Input.index' &lt;= 'Input.size'","     DO 'Output.Balances'['Input.index'] = 'Input.Balances'['Input.index']","     'Input.index' = 'Input.index' + 1","END_WHILE","Group characteristics","The following is an example of the syntax for using dynamic group characteristics in a script:","'Application.index' = 1","'Application.Total Amount' = 0","//for each applicant in the application","WHILE 'Application.index' &lt;= SIZE('Application.applicant') DO","     'Application.Account index' = 1","     'Application.applicant'['Application.index'].'Applicant Amount' = 0","     //total up the amounts on each account applied for","     WHILE 'Application.Account index' &lt;= SIZE('Application.applicant'['Application.index'].'Account') DO","          'Application.applicant'['Application.index'].'Applicant Amount' = 'Application.applicant'['Application.index'].'Applicant Amount' +       'Application.applicant'['Application.index'].'Account'['Application.Account index'].'Amount'","          'Application.Account index' = 'Application.Account index' + 1","          'Application.cardIndex' = 1","          'Application.applicant'['Application.index'].'cardsTotal' = 0","          WHILE 'Application.cardIndex' &lt;= SIZE('Application.applicant'['Application.index'].'cardLimits') DO","                'Application.applicant'['Application.index'].'cardsTotal' = 'Application.applicant'['Application.index'].'cardsTotal' + 'Application.applicant'['Application.index'].'cardLimits'['Application.cardIndex']","                'Application.cardIndex' = 'Application.cardIndex' + 1","          END_WHILE","          'Application.applicant'['Application.index'].'staticgrouparray'[2].'value' = 'Application.applicant'['Application.index'].'staticgrouparray'[1].'value' + 1","         'Application.applicant'['Application.index'].'staticleafarray'[2] = 'Application.applicant'['Application.index'].'staticleafarray'[1] + 1","     END_WHILE","     //add the total for this applicant to the running total","     'Application.Total Amount' = 'Application.Total Amount' + 'Application.applicant'['Application.index'].'Applicant Amount'","     'Application.index' = 'Application.index' + 1 ","END_WHILE","Limitations","Dynamic arrays characteristics can only be used in scripting components.","It is possible to define array elements in the script that are not within the bounds of the dynamic array. This is not reported at script compile time. For example there could be a reference to the dynamic characteristic element 20, but the actual (dynamically set) maximum size of the array could be 10.","Using dynamic arrays in a script","Usingdynamicarraysinascript.htm");
Page[12]=new Array("Operators or functions can be added to a script by using the auto complete functionality; by dragging and dropping from the Palette; or by creating the script freehand.","The script must be open for editing.","To add a function using auto complete","Click on the point in the script that you wish to add or insert the function. Place the cursor either at the beginning or end of the line.","Press the Ctrl+Space buttons to display the available functions.","A drop down list of all available logical data sources, characteristics, and functions is displayed. (See Using auto complete within a script for more details.)","Select the function you want to add, and press enter.","The function will be added to the script in addition to any parameters that are required by the function.","To add an operator or function to a script from the Palette","Click on the Expand (+) button in the Palette to expand either the Operators or Functions.","Drag the required function or operator and drop it onto the script at the required position.","The operator or function will be added to the script.","To add an operator or function to a script freehand","Type the operator or function in upper or case. ","Where the operator or function is followed by script text, ensure there is a space after the function or operator.","Where the operator or function is preceded by text, ensure there is a space before the function or operator.","The operator or function will be added to the script.","A OR B is valid","AORB is invalid.","Add an operator or function to a script","Addanoperatororfunctiontoascript.htm");
Page[13]=new Array("Users can create scripts more quickly by using auto complete to locate specific functions, data sources and characteristics. Auto complete is context sensitive, in that it takes into account the character preceding the cursor in filtering what options are displayed to the user.","To launch auto complete","Press Ctrl+Space to display the list of all available logical data sources, characteristics, and/or functions. ","or","Press the quote (') key to display only the list of available logical data sources.","Which logical data sources are displayed depends on the publishing rules associated with the folder in which you are creating the script. Logical data sources and characteristics are displayed in alphabetical order; functions are arranged in the same order in which they appear in the Palette.","Use the down arrow or mouse to select a data source or function from the list, and press enter. The data source or function is added to the script.","If a data source was selected:<br>With the cursor positioned after the data source name, press the full stop key (.) to display the list of available characteristics:","Use the down arrow or mouse to select a characteristic from the list, and press enter. The characteristic is added to the script.","If the selected characteristic contains further child characteristics (such characteristics are identified by a full stop (.) after the name), you can again press the full stop key (.) to display the list of available characteristics.","To Filter list contents","To filter the contents of a list, begin typing in the name of an item; the list of displayed items is narrowed as you type:","Use the down arrow or mouse to select an item from the list, and press enter. The item is added to the script.","You can continue using auto complete to build the script; for more information see using auto complete in context.","Use auto complete within a script","Useautocompletewithinascript.htm");
Page[14]=new Array("The contents of the auto complete drop down list depends on the position of the cursor in the line of script, and what text precedes the cursor. ","If you press Ctrl+Space at the beginning of a line, the drop down list appears with the list of all available logical data sources, characteristics, and functions. ","If you press the quote (') key, only the list of available logical data sources is displayed.","If you select a logical data source from the list, it will be entered into the script. If you then press the full stop, only the list of characteristics associated with that logical data source is displayed:","The nature of the characteristic is displayed: if it ends in a quote (&#8216;), it is a leaf characteristic; if it ends in a [ ] it is an array characteristic; if it ends in a full stop (.) there are further leaf characteristics after it.","Similarly, if you type the logical data source name into the script freehand (with no full stop after it), then press the full stop (.) key, only the list of characteristics associated with that logical data source is displayed.","Ctrl+Space can be used at any point in the script to launch auto-complete, and will calculate and display a list of possible options depending on the cursor position. If no auto-complete options are applicable then no list will be displayed.","When you have an array characteristic -- such as 'Application.Missing info'[ ] -- you can position the cursor within the brackets, and press the quote (') key, then select a logical data source and characteristic within the array brackets.","After completing a part of the script in the editor, you must add a space before Ctrl+Space or the quote (') key will again activate auto complete:","Using auto complete in context","Usingautocompleteincontext.htm");
Page[15]=new Array("The script must be open for editing.","To add a boolean expression to a script from the Resources window","Click on the Expand (+) button to display the contents of Boolean Expression in the Resources window.","Drag the required boolean expression and drop it onto the script at the required position.","The boolean expression will be added to the script.","The following is an example of how this will look in the script editor:<br>@","Add a boolean expression to a script","Addabooleanexpressiontoascript.htm");
Page[16]=new Array("A template is a helper for entering a language statement in a script.","The script must be open for editing.","To add a template to a script from the Palette","Click on the point in the script that you wish to add or insert the template.","Click on the Expand (+) button in the Palette to expand the Templates.","Drag the required template and drop it onto the script at the required position.","Replace the text and the chevrons with appropriate expressions, statements or constants.","The template will be added to the script.","To add a template to a script freehand","Type the required language statement ensuring that you follow the correct syntax.","There are templates for IF, IF..ELSE, Evaluate, Repeat and While language statements.","Add a template to a script","Addatemplatetoascript.htm");
Page[17]=new Array("The script must be open for editing.","To add a class set to a script from the Resources window","Click on the Expand (+) button to display the contents of the Class Set library in the Resources window.","Drag the required class set and drop it onto the script at the required position.","The class set will be added to the script.","The following is an example of how this will look in the script editor:<br>@","Add a class set to a script","Addaclasssettoascript.htm");
Page[18]=new Array("The script must be open for editing.","To add a matrix to a script from the Resources window","Click on the Expand (+) button to display the contents of the Matrix library in the Resources window.","Drag the required matrix and drop it onto the script at the required position.","The matrix will be added to the script.","The following is an example of how this will look in the script editor:<br>@","Add a matrix to a script","Addamatrixtoascript.htm");
Page[19]=new Array("The Resources window will only list those segmentation types that are valid for the script editor that is open.","The script must be open for editing.","To add a class set to a script","1.   Click on the Expand (+) button to display the contents of the Class Set library in the Resources window.","2.   Drag the required class set and drop it onto the script at the required position.","The class set will be added to the script.","The following is an example of how this will look in the script editor:<br>@","To add a boolean expression to a script","1.   Click on the Expand (+) button to display the contents of the Boolean Expression library in the Resources window.","2.   Drag the required boolean expression and drop it onto the script at the required position.","The boolean expression will be added to the script.","The following is an example of how this will look in the script editor:<br>@","To add a matrix to a script","1.   Click on the Expand (+) button to display the contents of the Matrix library in the Resources window.","2.   Drag the required matrix and drop it onto the script at the required position.","The matrix will be added to the script.","The following is an example of how this will look in the script editor:<br>@","Add segmentation to a script","Addsegmentationtoascript.htm");
Page[20]=new Array("Single text items or contiguous strings of text items can be copied and pasted in a script using standard keyboard copy and paste facilities.","To copy script item(s)","The script must be open for editing.","Highlight the required script item or string of items.","Press Ctrl+C to copy the item(s).","Click on the point in the script you wish to copy to.","Press Ctrl+V to paste.","The item(s) will be copied.","Copy items within a script","Copyitemswithinascript.htm");
Page[21]=new Array("Single text items or contiguous strings of text items can be moved within a script using standard keyboard cut and paste facilities.","To move script item(s)","The script must be open for editing.","Highlight the required script item or string of items.","Press Ctrl+X to cut the item(s).","Click on the point in the script you wish to move to.","Press Ctrl+V to paste.","The item will be moved.","Move items within a script","Moveitemswithinascript.htm");
Page[22]=new Array("Single text items or contiguous strings of text items can be deleted in a script using the delete button on the keyboard or the standard keyboard cut facility.","To delete script item(s)","The script must be open for editing.","Highlight the required script item or string of items.","Press Delete on the keyboard, or press Ctrl+X.","The item or string of items will be deleted.","Delete items within a script","Deleteitemswithinascript.htm");
Page[23]=new Array("The user can search for expressions, whole words or parts of words within a script.","The script editor must be open, the focus must be on the editor.","To perform a search/replace within a script","Press Ctrl+F to activate the search functionality at the bottom of the editor:","Type in the word or part of a word you want to find.","You can specify Match Case, find whole words only, display regular expressions, and highlight the results (the default).","By default, the results are highlighted in the script:","Click on Previous or Next to find other instances of a match.","Press Ctrl+H. <br>The standard Replace screen will be activated.","Carry on using the script editor as required.","Search/Replace within a script","Search_Replacewithinascript.htm");
Page[24]=new Array("The script syntax can be checked once the script has been created.","Script cannot be tested using Tester unless the script syntax is valid.","To check the script syntax","The script must be open for editing.","Click on the Compile Script @ button.","If the script is valid the following dialog will be displayed:","If the script is invalid the following dialog will be displayed:","@<br>A report of the errors will be displayed in the Output window if it is already open.","If the Output window is closed, click the OK button to close the Validation dialog.","From the Windows menu, select Output &gt; Output or use Ctrl+4 on your keyboard.<br>The Output window will be opened.<br>@","Click on the Compilation Report tab and click on the hyperlink.<br>The system will automatically move the cursor to the point in the script where the error has been found.","An error symbol @ is also displayed next to the faulty script. Hover the cursor over the error symbol to display the error message:","Amend the script as required, then use the Compile Script button again.","Check the script syntax","Checkthescriptsyntax.htm");
Page[25]=new Array("A line that has no effect is a line that is valid, but does not have an assignment at the left of a line (excluding the evaluation parts of IF, While and Repeat blocks, User Defined Functions, Sort, Merge and Return lines). This could arise, for example, if a statement such as:","'score' = 'Balance to limit' - 'Savings balance' - ('Monthly income' - 'Limit')","...is split into two lines by a carriage return:","'score' = 'Balance to limit' - 'Savings balance' ","- ('Monthly income' - 'Limit')","In this example &quot;- ('Monthly income' - 'Limit')&quot; is treated as a separate statement because it is on a separate line, and although it is a valid expression, it is considered to have zero effect because the result of the expression is not assigned to a characteristic.","The error message will read:","Script contains 'n' line(s) that have no effect.","A line that has no effect is a line that is valid, but does not have an assignment at the left of the line, excluding the evaluation parts of IF, EVALUATE, While and Repeat blocks, User Defined Functions, Sort, Merge and Return lines.","where 'n' will specify the number of lines in your script that have no effect.","Script validation error - Line has no effect","Scriptvalidationerror-Linehasnoeffect.htm");
Page[26]=new Array("A script must be saved before it can be used.","To save a script","To save any changes without exiting the editor click on the save @ icon.","Click on the the @ icon on the editor tab to close the script editor. If you have not saved already, you will be asked to save any changes made:","Click @ to save with errors.","Click @ to discard any changes made.","The script editor will close, saving the script.","Save a script","Saveascript.htm");
Page[27]=new Array("The derived data script editor will support the following:","Operators - 1 of 2","Statistical functions - 1 of 3","Text functions","Operators - 2 of 2","Statistical functions - 2 of 3","Value converters","Math functions","Statistical functions - 3 of 3","Templates","Array functions","Date and time functions","Operators and functions","Operatorsandfunctions.htm");
Page[28]=new Array("Basic Arithmetic Operators","Operator","Symbol","Usage (where Result is a logical data source characteristic)","Add","+","Result = Operand 1+ Operand 2","Assign","=","As shown in the above example. Assign is not applicable in a boolean expression or policy rule script.","Divide","/","Result = Operand 1 / Operand 2","Multiply","*","Result = Operand 1 * Operand 2","Percent","%","Result = Operand 1 % Operand 2 ","e.g., 30 = 15 % 200","Subtract","-","Result = Operand 1 - Operand 2","The standard order of precedence will be observed:","Brackets, Multiply, Divide, Percentage, Plus, Minus","Logical Operators","Operator","Symbol and Description","Usage ","Logical AND","AND","used to connect two statements where both are required to be true","A = B AND C = D","Logical OR","OR ","used to connect two statements where either one or the other or both are required to be true","A = B OR C = D","The logical operators AND and OR can be used to connect relational statements in a script. There is no precedence of one over the other; precedence is defined by brackets.","(Age &gt; 17 AND Income &gt; 1200) OR Age &gt; 25","Describes all people aged over 17 who earn more than 1200, together with anyone aged over 25.","Operators - 1 of 2","Operators_1of2.htm");
Page[29]=new Array("Comparison Operators","Operator","Symbol / Description","Usage","Equal ","=","Operand1 = Operand2","Excludes","EXCLUDES ","Array does not contain a specified value ","(Not compatible with Date fields)","Array1 EXCLUDES Operand2 ","where Array is a characteristic containing a list of data values (a table)","Greater than","&gt;","Operand1 &gt; Operand2","Greater than or equal ","&gt;=","Operand1 &gt;= Operand2","Includes","INCLUDES","Array contains a specified value","(Not compatible with Date fields)","Array1 INCLUDES Operand2 ","where Array1 is a characteristic containing a list of data values (a table)","e.g. Reason Code Table INCLUDES &quot;RR01&quot;","Inlist","INLIST","Array contains a specified value","Characteristic INLIST Array or Constant Array","where the value that exists in the characteristic is the value listed in the Array or the Constant Array","e.g. IF 'Employment Status' INLIST{&quot;FT&quot;,&quot;PT&quot;,&quot;SE&quot;} THEN","'Has Income'=1","ELSE","'Has Income'=0","ENDIF","Is null","ISNULL","Characteristic contains a &quot;Null&quot; value","ISNULL characteristic","where the value that exists in the characteristic is a &quot;Null&quot;","e.g. IF ISNULL 'Application Date'","THEN","'Date of Application' = SYSTEMDATE","ELSE","'Date of Application' = 'Application Date'","ENDIF","Less than","&lt;","Operand1 &lt; Operand2","Less than or equal","&lt;=","Operand1 &lt;= Operand2","Not equal ","&lt;&gt;","Operand1 &lt;&gt; Operand2","Further Operators are detailed in the Operators 1 of 2. Access the ISNULL handling for details on how to use this operator.","Operators - 2 of 2","Operators_2of2.htm");
Page[30]=new Array("In all of the following, expr is a numeric value, numeric characteristic or expression that returns a numeric value.","Function","Script Syntax","Mathematical Representation /Note","Absolute","Absolute Value","ABS( &lt;expr&gt; )","y = abs(expr)","Exec","Execute","EXEC( &quot;&lt;class.method&gt;&quot; )","This provides the means to execute external Java code. ","The parameter to the EXEC function is a string containing the fully qualified class name (i.e. including package) and method name. At runtime the class must be available on the classpath.","Please refer to the Decision Agent documentation for further information.","Exp","Exponential","EXP( &lt;expr&gt; )","Ln","Natural Logarithm","LN( &lt;expr&gt; )","y = ln(expr)","Log","LOG( &lt;expr&gt;)","y = log(expr)","Log n","Log to base n","LOG( &lt;expr&gt;, &lt;base&gt; )","Power","POWER( &lt;expr&gt;, &lt;power&gt; )","Random","RANDOM( &lt;Max&gt;)","This produces a number from 0 up to the number you have defined. Any positive number can be entered.","e.g., RANDOM(999) would produce a number from 0 to 998, RANDOM(5) would produce a number from 0 to 4.","Remainder","REM( &lt;expr&gt;, &lt;divisor&gt; )","y = REM (expr, divisor)","Divides the value in the expr by the divisor and places the remainder (if any) into y","e.g. REM (7,2) represents 7/2 = 3 rem 1, therefore 1 would be placed in y","Round down","Round up","Round nearest","Round nearest down","ROUNDD( &lt;expr&gt;, &lt;multiple&gt; )","ROUNDU( &lt;expr&gt;, &lt;multiple&gt; )","ROUNDN( &lt;expr&gt;, &lt;multiple&gt; )","ROUNDND( &lt;expr&gt;,&lt;multiple)","Where multiple is the value to be rounded to","Rounds a value Up/Down or to the Nearest multiple of &lt;multiple&gt;","When using round nearest, if the value is mid way between rounding up and rounding down, the default is to round up.  ","When using round near down, if the value is mid way between rounding up and rounding down, the system will round down.","e.g. ROUNDU(35.4,2) rounds up to the nearest 2, i.e. Y=36","ROUNDU(35.4,3) rounds up to the nearest 3, i.e. Y=37","ROUNDU(35.4,1) rounds up to the nearest 1, i.e. Y=35","When using negative numbers, rounding up means rounding up towards zero.","To numeric"," Value converters","Math functions","Mathfunctions.htm");
Page[31]=new Array("In a system where multiple decision setters are used at different points within the decisioning process, if a consolidated overall decision is required, then the individual decision results tables need to be merged together into a table producing the final top-ranking decision. Within the Derived Data Script component there is a specific function called Merge Tables. This function has been created to enable the user to merge multiple decision result tables to obtain the overall decision.","Other functions have been added to execute external calls, to execute external scripts, to generate unique IDs, to be able to persist multiple DA Call Results in a single instance, and to be able to obtain information about the operational environment.","Function","Script Syntax","Usage","Execute external call","EXEC( &quot;&lt;class.method&gt;&quot; )","Enables the user to call any Java code. The .jar file for the external code must be included on the Java Classpath used by the DA. NOTE: If the external call is used in interactive/non-interactive testing, the .jar file must be copied to a sub-folder of the Studio's installation folder.","Exect script","Execute script","EXEC_SCRIPT( &quot;&lt;script.filename&gt;&quot; )","Enables runtime capability of talking to external client-written scripts","Generate UUID","UUID()","User is able to invoke the unique ID generator. The function does not accept any parameters","Get Environment Variable","GETENV( &quot;&lt;variable_name&gt;&quot; )","Enables the solution designer to obtain information within the business process flow about the bank operator who operates on the Originations Runtime Server (BPS) and use it for either logging/tracing purposes or for executing boolean conditions. This function always yields a string, which can be either assigned to a logical data source characteristic or used as one side of a comparison. See Environment variable parameters for a list of all possible parameters that can be passed to the function.","Insert","INSERT( &quot;&lt;lds&gt;&quot;, '&lt;data view embedded array&gt;' )","Inserts logical data source characteristic into the embedded array logical data source characteristic ","Code Table Lookup","LOOKUPCODE (&lt;code table&gt;, &lt;desc table&gt;, &lt;decision reason code&gt;)","Returns the  descriptions corresponding to the given reason codes; looks up each of the reason codes from the specified Decision Reason Code Table and writes the description to the specified description table.","Code table =  Logical data source characteristic containing the list of reason codes. ","Desc table =  Logical data source characteristic to write the retrieved descriptions into. ","Decision Reason Code = The referenced Decision Reason Code Table component to use for the look up. ","Merge tables","MERGETABLES ( &lt;table1&gt;, &lt;table2&gt;, &lt;decision set&gt;, &lt;output table&gt;, &lt;decision category&gt;, &lt;decision text&gt;, &lt;reason code table&gt; )","Merges the contents of two decision setter tables, using the priority order defined in the decision set to produce a consolidated overall decision.","Reset","RESET( &quot;&lt;lds&gt;&quot; )","Initialises the lds value in memory state before running the next DA Call, so that it will contain only the new value to be inserted into the DA Result table","Other functions","Otherfunctions.htm");
Page[32]=new Array("The following is a list of all parameters that can be passed to the GETENV function, and a list of the system permissions that can be used with the SystemPermission parameter. All of the calls to GETENV return values that are taken from the operational user&#8217;s account fields. GETENV always returns values of type STRING, regardless of the parameter used.","Note these two known limitations:","1. Most of this information will not be available when external LDAP authentication is used, because in this case we don&#8217;t have access to the user account information.","2. When executing Screenless business process flows, the user does not select an active profile and group, so a GETENV call with the parameters UserActiveSecurityProfile or UserActiveGroup has no meaning.","In both of the above cases, if GETENV is used inappropriately it will simply yield an empty string and will not break the business process flow's execution.","Table 1: List of all possible parameters that can be passed to the function (only one per invocation):","Parameter","Description of Return Values for the Operational User(*)","Available in LDAP Authentication","TenantId","Returns the ID of the tenant from which the operational user operates","YES","UserId","Returns the User ID of the operational user","YES","UserName","Returns the first name","UserSurname","Returns the last name","UserGroups","Returns a comma separated list of all the groups the operational user is a member of","YES","UserBranches","Returns a comma separated list of all the branches of the operational user","YES","UserActiveSecurityProfile","Returns the profile under which the operational user currently acts","YES (Only in Web mode)","UserActiveGroup","Returns the group under which the operational user currently acts","YES (Only in Web mode)","UserEmail","Returns the email","UserAddress","Returns the Address","UserCity","Returns the City","UserCompany","Returns the Company","UserCountry","Returns the Country	","UserDepartment","Returns the Department","UserFax","Returns the Fax number","UserMobile","Returns the Mobile number","UserOffice","Returns the Office","UserPhone","Returns the Phone number","UserSecondFax","Returns the Second fax number","UserSecondEmail","Returns the Second email","UserSecondMobile","Returns the Second mobile number","UserSecondPhone","Returns the Second phone number","UserState","Returns the State of residence","UserTitle","Returns the Salutation","UserZip","Returns the ZIP code of residence","SystemPermission.&lt;System_Permission_Name&gt;","Returns &#8220;true&#8221; or &#8220;false&#8221; (as strings), depending on whether operational user has the specified system permission (see Table 2 below) allowed for the currently active profile.","YES","(*): The operational user currently executing the business objective flow in which the GETENV function is encountered. All the parameters actually retrieve information for this operational user.","Table 2: List of all system permissions that can be used in conjunction with &#8220;SystemPermission.&#8221; From Table 1:","Permission Name","Description (as seen in the Online Web Engine&#8217;s User Administration screen, English translation)","PERM_DATAVIEWER","Data Viewer","PERM_DATAVIEWER_PRINT","Data Viewer : Print","PERM_DYNAMIC_CREATE","Dynamic Parameters : Create","PERM_DYNAMIC_UPDATE","Dynamic Parameters : Update","PERM_DYNAMIC_VIEW","Dynamic Parameters : View","PERM_NOTE_CREATE","Notes : Create","PERM_NOTE_DELETE","Notes : Delete","PERM_NOTE_UPDATE","Notes : Update","PERM_NOTE_VIEW","Notes : View","PERM_OUA","Online User Administration","PERM_OUA_SECURITY_POLICY","Security Policy Administration","PERM_SOLUTION_ADMIN","Solution Administration","PERM_TACTICAL_ACCESS","Tactical Parameters : View","PERM_TACTICAL_CREATE_UPDATE","Tactical Parameters : Create/Update","PERM_TACTICAL_DEPLOY_SANCTION","Tactical Parameters : Deploy","PERM_VIEW_SENSITIVE_DATA","View sensitive data","Environment variable parameters","Environmentvariableparameters.htm");
Page[33]=new Array("These functions manipulate the contents of an array (table) characteristic. ","Note the following:","array is a single row table containing all text values or all numeric values.","dest is an array characteristic where the result of the function is to be placed.","dynamic array is a resizable array.","The ADDELEMENT, CLEAR and SETSIZE functions are only applicable for use with dynamic arrays. Dynamic arrays can be used with all other array functions.","bound is a limitation on the number of entries in the array on which the function will be based. For example a bound value of 10 will return the result based on the first 10 values. In the case of Max and Min, if no bound is entered then the function will be performed on all values in the array.","Function","Syntax","Usage","Add element","ADDELEMENT( &lt;dynamic array&gt; )","During execution ADDELEMENT increases the size of the dynamic array by 1. Initializes the new element values to NULL. ","Clear elements","CLEAR( &lt;dynamic array&gt; )","Reduces the dynamic array size to zero. ","Find","FIND( &lt;array&gt;, &lt;value&gt; )","value must be valid for the array type","Returns a number representing the location of the first matching value in the array","For example","location = FIND(array1,&quot;DE7&quot;)","Table entries start at location 1","Returns 0 if the value cannot be found","Max","MAX( &lt;array&gt;, &lt;bound&gt; )","Returns the largest value in the array","Merge","MERGE( &lt;array1&gt;, &lt;array2&gt;, &lt;order&gt;, &lt;dest&gt; )","order is:A (ascending), D (descending), AR (ascending remove duplicates), DR (descending remove duplicates)","Returns the combined and sorted data from two arrays","For example","MERGE (array1, array2, &quot;DR&quot;, array3)","Min","MIN( &lt;array&gt;, &lt;bound&gt; )","Returns the smallest value in the array","Size","SIZE( &lt;array&gt; )","Returns a numeric integer representing the size of an array, so you can perform nested looping through groups of data","For example","SIZE('App.Credit Card Limit')","Set Size","SETSIZE ( &lt;array&gt; , number )","*SETSIZE is a function to set the magnitude of a dynamic array.","For example","SETSIZE (&#8216;destination.group&#8217;, SIZE(&#8216;origin.group&#8217;) )","Sort","SORT( &lt;array&gt;, &lt;order&gt;, &lt;dest&gt; ) ","order is A, D, AR or DR as above ","Returns a sorted array","For example","SORT(array1,&quot;AR&quot;, array2)","Sum","SUM( &lt;array&gt;, &lt;bound&gt; )","Bound is a number or expression that represents the high water mark.","E.g. if 'bound' = 5, then the function calculates the sum of the first 5 values in the array.","Returns the sum of numeric values in a given numeric array.","To sum over the whole array you must enter the length of the array in 'bound'.","*SETSIZE is a companion function to ADDELEMENT.","SETSIZE should be used when the destination dynamic arrays magnitude can be pre-determined.","For example, when performing normalisation, going from a source logical data source to a destination logical data source, when only the format of the data needs to be changed, when occurrences of the data are not being added or removed.&nbsp; e.g. the size of the destination dynamic array will be the same as the size of the one which the function is reading from.","The &lt;array&gt; can be an atomic dynamic array or group dynamic array.&nbsp; The number can be a constant, a numeric characteristic, or the numeric result of another valid expression..","Array functions","Arrayfunctions.htm");
Page[34]=new Array("In all of the following:","array is a single row table characteristic containing numeric values","bound is a limitation on the number of entries in the array on which the function will be based. For example a bound value of 10 will return the result based on the first 10 values. If no bound is entered then the function will be performed on all values in the array.","Function","Script Syntax","Usage","Mean","MEAN( &lt;array&gt;, &lt;bound&gt; )","Returns the average value for the array","Median","MEDIAN( &lt;array&gt;, &lt;bound&gt; )","Returns the middle value in the array (when sorted ascending). Where there are an even number of values the average of the middle two will be returned.","Mode","MODE( &lt;array&gt;, &lt;bound&gt;, &lt;modality&gt;, &lt;modalValues&gt; )","See example below for detailed explanation","Returns the most common value in the array","Std","Standard Deviation","STD( &lt;array&gt;, &lt;bound&gt; )","Returns the standard deviation @ of the values held in the array","As MODE has a number of optional parameters (i.e., bound, modality, and modalValues) the following example will explain this function more clearly:","Where there is more than one most common value in the array, the first value (in ascending order) will be returned. A modality characteristic can optionally be entered to show how many most common values were found. A modalValues array characteristic can be entered to show what those most common values are.","If you write ","     'Most Common Value' = MODE ('Array 1', 100, 'How Many Values', 'Values' )","The script will evaluate the most common value in the first 100 values for 'Array 1'. In 'Array 1' there are two most common values; 215 and 400.","The values returned would therefore be:","     'Most Common Value' = 215","     'How Many Values' = 2","     'Values' = 215, 400","Statistical functions - 1 of 3","Statisticalfunctions_1of3.htm");
Page[35]=new Array("In all of the following:","array is a single row table characteristic containing numeric values","bound is a limitation on the number of entries in the array on which the function will be based. For example a bound value of 10 will return the result based on the first 10 values. If no bound is entered then the function will be performed on all values in the array","top is the number of minimum values to ignore","tail is the number of maximum values to ignore","toptaildev = number of standard deviations from the mean outside which values should be ignored","Function","Script Syntax","Usage","Mean top tail","MEANTT( &lt;array&gt;, &lt;bound&gt;, &lt;top&gt;, &lt;tail&gt; )","Returns the average of the values held in the array ignoring a number of maximum and minimum entries specified","Mean top tail standard","MEANTT2( &lt;array&gt;, &lt;bound&gt;, &lt;toptailstd&gt;)","Returns the average of the values held in the array ignoring entries falling outside the specified number of deviations from the mean","Std top tail","STDTT( &lt;array&gt;, &lt;bound&gt;, &lt;top&gt;, &lt;tail&gt; )","Returns the standard deviation of the values held in the array ignoring a number of maximum and minimum entries specified","Std top tail dev","STDTT2( &lt;array&gt;, &lt;bound&gt;, &lt;toptaildev&gt;)","Returns the standard deviation of the values held in the array ignoring entries falling outside the specified number of deviations from the mean","Result = MEANTT(array1,12,2,3) would calculate the mean of the first 12 values in array1 minus the two minimum and three maximum values (i.e., over the 7 remaining values).",".","Statistical functions - 2 of 3","Statisticalfunctions_2of3.htm");
Page[36]=new Array("In both of the following, the statistical function uses a number:","Function","Script Syntax","Usage","Normal distribution","NORMSDIST( &lt;expr&gt; )","Uses the cumulative normal probability distribution to return the probability of a result that lies &lt;expr&gt; or more standard deviations above the mean.","Norms inv","NORMSINV( &lt;expr&gt; )","Returns the number of standard deviations above the mean that an observation would have to be in order to have the input probability.","Cumulative Normal Distribution","NORMSDIST( &lt;expr&gt; )","Uses the cumulative normal probability distribution to return the probability of a result that lies &lt;expr&gt; or more standard deviations above the mean. A negative number denotes the number of standard deviations below the mean, but the probability returned is still the probability that the result lies at or above the chosen point.","Parameters: ( Real ) Return: ( Real between 0 and 1 )","NORMSDIST( 0 ) = 0.5","NORMSDIST( 1 ) = 0.841. . .","NORMSDIST( -1 ) = 0.158. . .","NORMSDIST( 2 ) = 0.977. . .","NORMSDIST( x ) = 1 - NORMSDIST( -x )","Inverse Cumulative Normal Distribution","NORMSINV( &lt;expr&gt; )","Is the inverse of the NORMSDIST function. Returns the number of standard deviations above the mean that an observation would have to be in order to have the input probability.","Parameters: ( Real between 0 and 1) Return: ( Real )","NORMSINV( 0.95 ) = 1.644. . .","NORMSINV( 0.841… ) = 1","NORMSINV( 0.158… ) = -1","NORMSINV( 0.5 ) = 0","NORMSINV( 0 ) and NORMSDIST( 1 ) are both infinitely large, and so will produce incorrect results.","Statistical functions - 3 of 3","Statisticalfunctions_3of3.htm");
Page[37]=new Array("Manipulate date type characteristics or explicitly entered dates or time characteristics. ","Dates entered explicitly must be in the format CCYYMMDD. Date characteristics will be of the format supplied in the data. Time characteristics will return a STRING.","Function","Script Syntax","Note","Date Change","DATE( &lt;givendate&gt;, &lt;period&gt; )","period is number of days as a: constant, numeric characteristic or expression ","givendate is a logical data source date type","Returns a date relative to a given date by the number of days specified by &lt;period&gt;","e.g. enddate = DATE(startdate, 30 )","startdate = DATE(enddate, - 90 )","Days Between ","DAYS( &lt;date1&gt;, &lt;date2&gt; )","date1 and date2 are logical data source date types or expressions that resolve to date types","Returns a numeric value representing the number of days between two dates ","e.g. noofdays = DAYS( start, end )","Day of week","number = DAYOFWEEK( &lt;date&gt;)","date is a logical data source date type.","number is a logical data source numeric characteristic","This function returns the day of the week for a given date","e.g. 5 =DAYOFWEEK (TODATE(&quot;19640417&quot;))","1=Monday, 7=Sunday therefore the above day is a Friday","Months Between","MONTHS( &lt;date1&gt;, &lt;date2&gt; )","date1 and date2 are logical data source date types or expressions that resolve to date types","Returns the number of whole months between two dates; if the dates of the months are the same it returns 1 <br>e.g., <br>MONTHS (TODATE(&quot;20030701&quot;) , TODATE(&quot;20030314&quot;)) will return -3","MONTHS (TODATE(&quot;20030722&quot;) , TODATE(&quot;20030822&quot;)) will return 1","MONTHS (TODATE(&quot;20030722&quot;) , TODATE(&quot;20030821&quot;)) will return 0","System date","SYSTEMDATE( &lt;const&gt;)","const is a: constant, numeric characteristic or expression ","Returns a date relative to the current date by the number of days specified by &lt;const&gt;","e.g. D = SYSTEMDATE(0) is todays date","D = SYSTEMDATE(-1) is yesterdays date","System date time","SYSTEMDATETIME()","Returns the current date and time in the format ","YYMMDD HH:MM:SS (24 hour clock) to a STRING. The STRING needs to be a length of 17.","e.g. 20080304 13.:24:15","System time","SYSTEMTIME()","Returns the current time in the format HH:MM:SS (24 hour clock) to a STRING. The STRING needs to be a length of 8.","e.g. 13:24:15","To date","Value converters","Date and time functions","Dateandtimefunctions.htm");
Page[38]=new Array("In all of the following:","char is a text characteristic containing a string of characters","value can be a characteristic, string, number or expression","Function","Script Syntax","Note","Concatenate","STRING( &lt;value1&gt;, &lt;value2&gt; )","This function returns a character string that represents the contents of value1 and value2 concatenated","Substring","SUBSTRING( &lt;char&gt;, &lt;start&gt; , &lt;length&gt;)","This function returns a character string containing a set of characters out of another string","e.g., newstring = SUBSTRING(oldstr,1,5)","returns the first five characters contained in 'oldstr' and places them in 'newstring'","Trim","TRIM( &lt;char&gt;)","This function returns a character string with leading and trailing blanks removed","To date","See Value converters","To numeric","See Value converters","To string","See Value converters","Text functions","Textfunctions.htm");
Page[39]=new Array("These functions convert the values from another data type to that defined.","Function","Syntax","Usage","To date","TODATE('AppData.Numeric')","Can convert a numeric or string to a date. If a constant value is entered it must be a valid date in the format CCYYMMDD. A value in a different format will cause an error at runtime.","For example","TODATE(&quot;20010110&quot;) = 20010110","To string","TOSTRING('AppData.Numeric')","Can convert a numeric or date to a string. ","For example","TOSTRING(15) = &quot;15&quot;","To numeric","TONUMERIC('AppData.String')","Can convert a string or date to numeric.","For example","TONUMERIC(&quot;25&quot;) = 25","Value converters","Valueconverters.htm");
Page[40]=new Array("Evaluate is a shorthand way of writing nested IF statements. It allows the comparison of one or more expressions with an initial expression. The first comparison that evaluates to true will result in a statement being performed.","To set an Income Bracket description based on the values held in an Income characteristic you may write:","     EVALUATE 'Generic App.Income'","     WHEN &gt; 3000 DO 'Generic App.Income Bracket' = &quot;High&quot;","     WHEN &gt; 1500 DO 'Generic App.Income Bracket' = &quot;Middle&quot;","     OTHER 'Generic App.Income Bracket' = &quot;Low&quot;","     END_EVALUATE","        - If the value in Income is greater than 3000 set the Income Bracket to a value of &quot;High&quot;","        - If the value in Income is greater than 1500 set the Income Bracket to a value of &quot;Middle&quot;","        - Otherwise set the Income Bracket to a value of &quot;Low&quot;","The Evaluate syntax is:","EVALUATE &lt;expr&gt;","WHEN &lt;comp&gt; &lt;expr&gt; DO &lt;stmt&gt; (WHEN....DO... is repeated as often as required)","OTHER &lt;stmt&gt;","END_EVALUATE","In the above example:","'Generic App.Income' replaces the initial &lt;expr&gt; in the supplied template","&gt; replaces the &lt;comp&gt; in the supplied template","3000 replaces the &lt;expr&gt; in the WHEN..DO... &lt;expr&gt; in the supplied template","'Generic App.Income Bracket' = &quot;High&quot; replaces the &lt;stmt&gt; in the supplied template","The second WHEN...DO.. line is added to the initial template","'Generic App.Income Bracket' = &quot;Low&quot; replaces the &lt;stmt&gt; after the OTHER in the supplied template","Generally:","An initial expression is entered. This expression can be a characteristic or a calculation but must result in a value","Then a series of WHEN statements are written to make a comparison against the initial expression. The expression being compared can be a characteristic or a calculation but must have the same data type as the initial expression","The first WHEN comparison that produces a true result will cause the DO statement that follows it to be executed ","If none of the WHEN comparisons produce a true result then the OTHER statement is processed","The OTHER statement is not optional, if it is not included the script will not compile properly","The expressions used in the WHEN.. DO.. lines could overlap and so the order in which they are written is important as the statement on the first true condition will be performed.","For example in above you would not write &gt;1500 before &gt;3000 as if it is &gt;3000 it will also be &gt;1500 and the statement relating to 1500 will be processed even if the value is, for example 4000.","EVALUATE WHEN","EVALUATEWHEN.htm");
Page[41]=new Array("IF statements perform a defined action if a defined condition is true.","The syntax is:","IF &lt;expr&gt; THEN","&lt;stmt&gt;","ENDIF","The &lt;expr&gt; is an expression which sets a condition, which if true allows the statement that follows to be performed. If the condition is false the statement that follows will not be performed","The &lt;expr&gt; part of the template should be replaced by an appropriate expression applying a logical comparison","The &lt;stmt&gt; should be replaced by the action that is to be performed if the previous condition is true","IF 'Generic App.Age' &gt; 17 THEN","'Results.Credit Limit' = 3 * 'Generic App.Income'","ENDIF","   - 'Generic App.Age' &gt; 17 has replaced the &lt;expr&gt; in the supplied template","   - 'Results.Credit Limit' = 3 * 'Generic App.Income' has replaced the &lt;stmt&gt; in the supplied template"," The above script sets the applicant's credit limit at 3 times their income providing the applicant is aged over 17.","IF","IF.htm");
Page[42]=new Array("IF...THEN...ELSE statements perform a defined action if a defined condition is true and an alternative action if the condition is false.","The syntax is:","IF &lt;expr&gt; THEN","&lt;stmt&gt;","ELSE","&lt;stmt&gt;","ENDIF","The &lt;expr&gt; is an expression which sets a condition, which if true allows the statement that follows to be performed. If the condition is false the statement that follows the ELSE will be performed.","The &lt;expr&gt; part of the template should be replaced by an appropriate expression applying a logical comparison.","The &lt;stmt&gt; following THEN should be replaced by the action that is to be performed if the set condition is true.","The &lt;stmt&gt; following ELSE should be replaced by the action that is to be performed if the set condition is false.","IF 'Generic App.Age' &gt; 17 THEN ","'Results.Credit Limit' = 3 * 'Generic App.Income' ","ELSE","'Results.Credit Limit' = 0","ENDIF","   - 'Generic App.Age' &gt; 17 has replaced the &lt;expr&gt; in the supplied template.","   - 'Results.Credit Limit' = 3 * 'Generic App.Income' has replaced the first &lt;stmt&gt; in the supplied template.","   - 'Results.Credit Limit' = 0 has replaced the second &lt;stmt&gt; in the supplied templateype your text here.","The above script sets the applicant's credit limit at 3 times his income providing the applicant is aged over 17, if the applicant is under 17 the credit limit will be set at zero.",".","IF THEN ELSE","IFTHENELSE.htm");
Page[43]=new Array("Repeat performs some action repetitively until a terminating condition becomes true. You can optionally set a limit on the number of times the action can be repeated. ","The syntax is:","REPEAT &lt;stmt&gt; ","UNTIL &lt;expr&gt; LIMIT &lt;const&gt; ","END_REPEAT","&lt;stmt&gt; should be replaced by an action to be performed","&lt;expr&gt; should be replaced by a condition, that if it becomes true will end the process)","LIMIT is optional and if present:","&lt;const&gt; should be replaced by a numeric value - the maximum number of repetitions","'temp.arrayIndex' = 1","REPEAT","     'results.array'['temp.arrayIndex']' = 0","    'temp.arrayIndex' = 'temp.arrayIndex' + 1","UNTIL 'temp.arrayIndex' = 10 ","END_REPEAT","The above script is initialising each element in a table (array) to zero. An index is set to 1 (note this must be a characteristic that already exists in the logical data source) and is used to reference the array fields being initialised ( see [ ] in above). The index and subsequently the array field is incremented as part of the Repeat process. The process is repeated until the index has reached a value of 10 (the number of elements in the array).","REPEAT always performs the action at least once, it will perform the action and then check to see if the UNTIL expression is true and then check if the LIMIT has been reached.","REPEAT UNTIL","REPEATUNTIL.htm");
Page[44]=new Array("WHILE repeatedly performs an action while a condition remains true. You can optionally set a limit on the number of times the action can be repeated. However, if you do not specify the limit, loops within scripts will be limited to 100 iterations.","The syntax is:","WHILE &lt;expr&gt;","DO &lt;expr&gt; ","LIMIT &lt;const&gt;","END_WHILE","The first &lt;expr&gt; should be replaced by a condition that must be true for the action to be performed","The second &lt;expr&gt; should be replaced by an action to be performed","LIMIT is optional and if present:","&lt;const&gt; should be replaced by a numeric value - the maximum number of repetitions","For Example:","'temp.array.Index' = 1","WHILE 'results.decision_code'['temp.arrayIndex'] &lt;&gt; &quot;D&quot;","DO 'results.decision_code'['temp.arrayIndex'] = &quot;A&quot;","'temp.arrayIndex' = 'temp.arrayIndex' + 1","LIMIT 10","END_WHILE","The above script will change all of the values in an array (table) to &quot;A&quot; unless an original value of &quot;D&quot; is found. When &quot;D&quot; is found no further values will be changed. The array has 10 elements and so this is the limit on the processing. An index is set to 1 (note this must be a characteristic that already exists in the logical data source) and is used to reference the array fields being checked ( see [ ] in above). The index and subsequently the array field is incremented as part of the While process.","WHILE may never perform the action. It will check the condition first and if it is false the action will never be performed.",".","WHILE DO","WHILEDO.htm");
Page[45]=new Array("This topic details the results that can be expected when using the ISNULL function for the following data types:","Numeric Characteristics (Byte Array)","String Characteristics (Byte Array)","Date Characteristics (Byte Array)","Java Data Types","ISNULL Handling - Numeric Characteristics (Byte Array)","The ISNULL script function will return the following results when the characteristic contains something other than a number. Non-numeric values will generate an exception if referenced in any other script.","Format","ISNULL result when low-values","ISNULL result when spaces","ADNL","True","False","ADNT","True","False","AZDL","True","False","AZDT","True","False","AZDU","True","False","DNL","True","False","DNT","True","False","PD","True","False","ZDL","True","False","ZDT","True","False","ZDS","True","False","ZDU","True","False","The behaviour of floating point and binary characteristics with respect to ISNULL script processing is summarised below. With these data types, all values are interpreted as valid numbers:","Format","ISNULL result when low-values","ISNULL result when spaces","BEF","False","False","LEF","False","False","PCF","False","False","MFBS","False","False","MFBU","False","False","PCBS","False","False","PCBU","False","False","Low-values (also known as null) is represented in hexadecimal as X&#8217;00&#8217;.","The space character is represented in hexadecimal as X&#8217;40&#8217; (z/OS and OS/390) or X&#8217;20&#8217; (Windows and Unix operating systems).","ISNULL Handling - String Characteristics (Byte Array)","The ISNULL script function will return the following result for String data types that contain &#8216;white space&#8217; characters:","Format","ISNULL result when low-values","ISNULL result when spaces","Any","False","False","Low-values (also known as null) is represented in hexadecimal as X&#8217;00&#8217;.","The space character is represented in hexadecimal as X&#8217;40&#8217; (CE data type and EBCDIC encodings) or X&#8217;20&#8217; (CA and UTF data types, ASCII and Unicode encodings).","ISNULL Handling &#8211; Date Characteristics (Byte Array)","The ISNULL script function will return the following results for characteristics that are assigned a date format but contain something other than a date. ","The ADNL, ADNT, DNL and DNT data types can not have an associated date format, as they contain an explicit sign character (+/-).","Numeric data formats:","Format","ISNULL result when low-values","ISNULL result when spaces","AZDL","True","True","AZDT","True","True","AZDU","True","True","BEF","True","False","LEF","True","False","MFBS","True","False","MFBU","True","False","PCBS","True","False","PCBU","True","False","PCF","True","False","PD","True","False","ZDL","True","True","ZDT","True","True","ZDS","True","True","ZDU","True","True","Low-values (also known as null) is represented in hexadecimal as X&#8217;00&#8217;.","The space character is represented in hexadecimal as X&#8217;40&#8217; (EBCDIC z/OS and OS/390) or X&#8217;20&#8217; (Windows and Unix operating systems).","String data formats:","Format","ISNULL result when low-values","ISNULL result when spaces","Any","True","True","Low-values (also known as null) is represented in hexadecimal as X&#8217;00&#8217;.","The space character is represented in hexadecimal as X&#8217;40&#8217; (CE data format and any EBCDIC code page) or X&#8217;20&#8217; (CA and UTF data formats and any ASCII or Unicode code page). ","ISNULL Handling &#8211; Java Data Types","The ISNULL script function will return the following result for Java data types:","Format","ISNULL result when low-values","ISNULL result when spaces","String","True","False","Numeric","True","False","Date","True","False","ISNULL handling","ISNULLhandling.htm");
var PageCount=46;

function search(SearchWord){
var Result="";
var NrRes=0;
Result='<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC "-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01 Transitional//EN" "http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/loose.dtd">\n';
Result+="<html>\n";
Result+="<head>\n";
Result+="<title>Search Results</title>\n";
Result+="<meta http-equiv='Content-Type' content='text/html; charset=UTF-8'>\n";
Result+='<script language="javascript" type="text/javascript" charset="UTF-8" src="dhtml_search.js"></script>\n';
Result+='<link rel="stylesheet" type="text/css" href="stylesheet.css">\n';
Result+="<style type='text/css'>\n";
Result+=".searchDetails {font-family:verdana; font-size:8pt; font-weight:bold}\n";
Result+=".searchResults {font-family:verdana; font-size:8pt}\n";
Result+="</style>\n";
Result+="</head>\n";
Result+="<body onload='javascript:document.SearchForm.SearchText.focus()'>\n";
Result+='<table class="searchDetails" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="2" width="100%">\n';
Result+='<tr><td>Enter a keyword or phrase</td></tr>';
Result+='<tr><td>';
Result+='<form name="SearchForm" action="javascript:search(document.SearchForm.SearchText.value)">';
if(SearchWord.length>=1){
   while(SearchWord.indexOf("<")>-1 || SearchWord.indexOf(">")>-1 || SearchWord.indexOf('"')>-1){
       SearchWord=SearchWord.replace("<","&lt;").replace(">","&gt;").replace('"',"&quot;");
   }
}
Result+='<input type="text" name="SearchText" size="25" value="' + SearchWord + '" />';
Result+='&nbsp;<input type="submit" value="&nbsp;Go&nbsp;"/></form>';
Result+='</td></tr></table>\n';

if(SearchWord.length>=1){
   SearchWord=SearchWord.toLowerCase();
   this.status="Searching, please wait...";
   Result+="<table border='0' cellpadding='5' class='searchResults' width='100%'>";
   for(j=0;j<PageCount;j++){
       k=Page[j].length-1;
       for(i=0;i<k;i++){
           WordPos=Page[j][i].toLowerCase().indexOf(SearchWord);
           if(WordPos>-1){
               FoundWord=Page[j][i].substr(WordPos,SearchWord.length);
               NrRes++;
               Result+="<tr><td>";
               Result+="<a target='BODY' href='"+Page[j][k]+"'>"+Page[j][k-1].replace(FoundWord,FoundWord.bold())+"</a><br/>\n";

               if(i<k-1){
                   if(Page[j][i].length>350){
                       Result+="..."+Page[j][i].substr(WordPos-100,200+FoundWord.length).replace(FoundWord,FoundWord.bold())+"...\n";
                   }
                   else{
                       Result+=Page[j][i].replace(FoundWord,FoundWord.bold())+"\n";
                   }
               }
               Result+="</td></tr>";
               break;
           }
       }
   }
   Result+="</table>";
   Result+="<p class='searchDetails'>&nbsp;" + NrRes + " result(s) found.</p>";
}

Result+="</body></html>";
this.status="";
this.document.open();
this.document.write(Result);
this.document.close();
}